# Native client (sfcop --input; oracle/driver/run_native.sh --steps): boot to the main menu, open
# Multiplayer, take the LAN (TCP/IP) path to the session browser, wait there with the list empty,
# then host a game and reach the player list ("Multiplayer Startup") with the host shown. With
# multiplayer-join.steps in a second client, the second player joins this game. Needs a data
# folder with a stored key.
#
# The waits on screens are marks the lift adds only when the build is configured with them
# (src/app/input/README.md, "waitmark"):
#
#   -DSFCOP_LIFT_EXTRA_MARKS=0x0046667A,0x00464D4F,0x00461C67,0x0046ED6A
#
# each the entry (vfunction2) of a screen's state, as the Select Game and Setup marks are:
#   0x0046667A  tState_GameConnections       "Game Connections", the Multiplayer screen
#   0x00464D4F  tState_GameBrowser           "Select Game", the session browser
#   0x00461C67  tState_CustomizeMultiplayer  "Create Multiplayer Game"
#   0x0046ED6A  tState_Multiplayer           "Multiplayer Startup", the player list
# A build without them runs out of time at the first of these waits and exits 2.
#
# Coordinates are the game's display pixels (800x600, the 640x480 menu centred), as in
# menu.steps. Calibrated on the native build, 2026-11-08, with --shots captures of each screen.

window 60 Starfleet Command

# --- the main menu, "Select Game" (60 s until the boot time is fixed; menu.steps says why)
waitmark 90 Select Game
sleep 1000

# --- MULTIPLAYER opens Game Connections. Entering it lists DirectPlay's connections
# (STARFLEETOP 0x00614520): the screen offers TCP/IP and greys IPX.
click 563 348
waitmark 15 0x0046667A
sleep 2000

# --- LAN CONNECTIONS, TCP/IP: the session browser, which starts enumerating the LAN at once
click 487 322
waitmark 15 0x00464D4F

# --- with no host on the network the list stays empty and the screen stays live: the frames
# go on while the enumeration runs (the captures show it at once and after ten seconds)
sleep 10000

# --- CREATE: Create Multiplayer Game, with the game's default name, scenario and options
click 456 506
waitmark 15 0x00461C67
sleep 3000

# --- ANNOUNCE GAME: the session is created on the LAN and the host's player made; the player
# list opens with the host in the first row
click 612 302
waitmark 15 0x0046ED6A

# --- the host stays in the player list for the joiner (multiplayer-join.steps)
sleep 60000
